 165 G for newcomer with cursed sword: 0 years, first insurance -- matches integration example\n43. should calculate premium 160 G for long-standing customer's second contract with cursed sword, enchantment 7 -- matches integration example\n\nTest List Phase Complete. Proceeding to Red phase with the first test.\n\n## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim operations\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 42\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should return premium 5 G for empty item list -- only processing fee\n2. should have base premium 100 G for a sword\n3. should have base premium 60 G for an amulet\n4. should have base premium 80 G for a staff\n5. should have base premium 40 G for a potion\n6. should have base premium 25 G per component (rune or moonstone)\n7. should apply 50% risk surcharge for cursed items\n8. should apply 30% risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment ≥ 5)\n9. should apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with ≥ 2 years with MHPCO\n10. should apply 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance\n11. should apply 15% discount for contracts after the first\n12. should add 5 G processing fee to every premium\n13. should offer special base premium of 60 G for a building block of 3 alike components\n14. should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- base premium 100 G\n15. should have base premium 175 G for 7 runes -- no block\n16. should not apply block discount for 2 runes + 1 moonstone -- base premium 75 G, different types\n17. should apply two separate blocks for 3 runes + 3 moonstones -- base premium 120 G\n18. should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed sword's base premium in a multi-item policy with cursed sword and plain amulet -- surcharge adds 50 G\n19. should apply loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years with MHPCO\n20. should apply high-enchantment surcharge for sword with exactly enchantment 5\n21. should not apply high-enchantment surcharge for sword with enchantment 4\n22. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event\n23. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n24. should reimburse 50% of damage amount for items with enchantment level ≥ 8\n25. should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material\n26. should fully reimburse regular sword (enchantment 3), damage 500 G -- payout 400 G\n27. should reimburse 100 G for damage to a rune, damage 200 G -- full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible\n28. should apply both dragon-material and high-enchantment clauses: dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -- payout 400 G (50% rule wins, then deductible)\n29. should fully reimburse dragon-material sword, enchantment 5"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784951613001,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c616a4cf-0dbf-4b7a-b71f-ade5e954320a","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Test List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office - quote and claim operations\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 42\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should return premium 5 G for empty item list -- only processing fee\n2. should have base premium 100 G for a sword\n3. should have base premium 60 G for an amulet\n4. should have base premium 80 G for a staff\n5. should have base premium 40 G for a potion\n6. should have base premium 25 G per component (rune or moonstone)\n7. should apply 50% risk surcharge for cursed items\n8. should apply 30% risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment ≥ 5)\n9. should apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with ≥ 2 years with MHPCO\n10. should apply 10% initial assessment surcharge fo