ance sum\n24. should reimburse 50% of damage amount for items with enchantment level ≥ 8\n25. should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material\n26. should fully reimburse regular sword (enchantment 3), damage 500 G -- payout 400 G\n27. should reimburse 100 G for damage to a rune, damage 200 G -- full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible\n28. should apply both dragon-material and high-enchantment clauses: dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -- payout 400 G (50% rule wins, then deductible)\n29. should fully reimburse dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -- payout 700 G (dragon-material clause applies, then deductible)\n30. should reimburse steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -- payout 400 G (high-enchantment clause applies: 50% first, then deductible)\n31. should cover two swords in policy: insurance sum 2000 G, cap 4000 G\n32. should apply separate deductible for each damaged item in dragon attack on two insured swords\n33. should reject claim if damages contain more entries of a type than policy covers -- e.g. two sword damages but only one sword insured\n34. should set policy cap to 2000 G for a cursed sword -- based on unmodified insurance value, cap is twice insurance sum\n35. should set insurance sum to 1750 G for policy with sword and 3 runes (block) -- block discount affects premium only, not insurance sum\n36. should reduce second claim payout to remaining cap: first claim 1400 G, cap remaining 600 G; second claim desired 1400 G reduced to 600 G, cap 0\n37. should round premium calculation in MHPCO's favor: 197.5 G yields 198 G\n38. should round payout calculation in MHPCO's favor: 350.5 G yields 350 G\n39. should exit with non-zero status code for quote with unknown item type (e.g. broomstick)\n40. should exit with non-zero status code for claim referencing damage entry not part of policy\n41. should exit with non-zero status code for claim with negative damage amount (e.g. -200)\n42. should calculate premium